== 2. RUNTIME CHECK ==
Command (from mobile/):  bun run smoke:runtime   (= scripts/runtime-smoke.sh [bundle-file|bundle-url])
  - With no arg: `npx expo export --platform ios --no-bytecode` into a temp dir, then runs the bundle.
  - With a URL/file: runs that bundle (used below against the bundle host's launchAsset).
  - scripts/runtime-smoke.mjs executes the production iOS JS bundle in Node with fake Fabric UIManager,
    TurboModules and Expo modules (SecureStore returns a token or null), starts it via
    RN$AppRegistry.runApplication("main"), and fails on any fatal JS exception or if the expected first
    screen (Chat with a token, Setup without) is not committed to the fake native view tree.
  - Fix to the handed-over draft: the fake RNCSafeAreaProvider now fires topInsetsChange (the real native
    view does after layout); without it safe-area-context rendered no children and nothing past the root mounted.
